                <invention-title lang="de">ERWEITERTE ANALYTISCHE UND DIAGNOSTISCHE SYSTEME UND VERFAHREN FÜR INTELLIGENTE BATTERIEN</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="fr">ALIMENTATION SANS COUPURE ET SUPPORT NON TRANSITOIRE LISIBLE PAR ORDINATEUR
</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="en">UNINTERRUPTIBLE POWER SUPPY AND NON-TRANSITORY COMPUTER-READABLE MEDIUM</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A method of controlling an uninterruptible power supply including an input to receive input power, a battery input to receive battery power from a battery, an output to provide output power derived from at least one of the input power or the battery power, and at least one interface configured to receive first sensor data indicative of operating information of the battery and second sensor data indicative of state-of-health characteristics of the battery from one or more sensors, and configured to communicate with a computer system coupled to a plurality of uninterruptible power supplies, the method comprising receiving the first sensor data from the one or more sensors; providing the first sensor data to the computer system; receiving an estimated battery health status of the battery from the computer system, the estimated battery health status being determined based on the first sensor data and baseline battery health characteristics stored by the computer system by using the operating information as an input to the baseline battery health characteristics to determine the estimated battery health status; receiving the second sensor data from the one or more sensors; determining an actual battery health status of the battery based on the second sensor data; comparing the estimated battery health status and the actual battery health status of the battery; and communicating adjustment information to the computer system to adjust the baseline battery health characteristics based at least in part on the comparison of the estimated battery health status and the actual battery health status.</p>
            </abstract>
